      "content": "fair enough. but looking at the actual substance, do you think the arguments for regulation are actually stronger? like, some critics say the 'innovation' defense is just a hollow shield to protect monopolies, whereas the actual data on market concentration is pretty undeniable. does the lack of real competition actually make the legal case for antitrust more concrete?",
